@* A row that is still on its way (an image being pulled, a run waiting for its
   image), in its Name cell: the name, the
   percentage, the console and cancel while it runs, the bar under them. A
   failed one keeps the bar in the error colour, says why in its tooltip, keeps
   the console when its output has the reason, and its cross becomes Dismiss:
   the agent remembers a failure for a while, and the row must not outlive the
   user's interest in it. One that ended well, for as long as it is still
   listed, has the bar whole and its cross in the success colour: it is over,
   it went well, and the cross only closes it. What a list puts before a
   row's name (a group's +/−, the mark of a row that stands under one) goes
   before it here too (Lead). Work that has no measure of how far it is (a
   container being started or stopped) has the bar moving from end to end and
   no percentage (Indeterminate); a row that only waits its turn has the bar
   whole and still, without one either (ShowPct). A stop's moving bar runs
   from right to left (Reversed). A row with nothing to
   cancel or to dismiss has no cross: a cross that does nothing is worse
   than none. *@

<div title="@Status" class="wslc-progress-cell @(Mixed ? "wslc-progress-mixed" : "") @(Reversed ? "wslc-progress-reversed" : "")">
    <MudStack Row="true" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Spacing="1" Wrap="Wrap.NoWrap">
        @Lead
        <span class="wslc-progress-name">@Name</span>
        @if (Running && ShowPct && !Indeterminate)
        {
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mud-text-secondary wslc-progress-pct">@(Pct)%</MudText>
        }
        @* No console, no button: an upload is bytes on their way, not output
           to read, and a magnifier that opens nothing is worse than none. *@
        @if (OnLog.HasDelegate && (Running || LogAfterFailure))
        {
            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Subject" Size="Size.Small" title="@LogTitle" aria-label="@LogTitle" OnClick="OnLog" />
        }
        @if ((Running ? OnCancel : OnDismiss).HasDelegate)
        {
            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Close" Size="Size.Small" Color="@(Done ? Color.Success : Color.Error)" title="@(Running ? CancelTitle : DismissTitle)" aria-label="@(Running ? CancelTitle : DismissTitle)"
                           OnClick="@(Running ? OnCancel : OnDismiss)" />
        }
    </MudStack>
    @* Info, the ring's blue in the cards: the same work in the same colour in both views. *@
    <MudProgressLinear Indeterminate="@(Running && Indeterminate)" Value="@(Running ? Math.Max(Pct, 2) : 100)" Color="@(Done ? Color.Success : Failed ? Color.Error : Color.Info)" Size="Size.Small" />
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Name { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>What stands before the name in this row, when its list puts something there.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Lead { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public int Pct { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The work says how far it has got, and the row says it as a percentage; false for a bar that only stands there (a row waiting its turn).</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool ShowPct { get; set; } = true;

    /// <summary>The work has no measure of how far it is: the bar moves from end to end, and no percentage is said.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Indeterminate { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The work is a stop: the bar is drawn from the right, so it runs from right to left.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Reversed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The step under way, or why it failed.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Status { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter] public bool Failed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>It ended well and is still listed: drawn whole in the success colour, its cross closing it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Done { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The work is a project's, some of its containers up and some not yet: the bar in both colours, the running one and the stopped one, as its card's ring is.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Mixed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the console still has something to read once the row ended: a pull's output does, a run that failed after its pull has none.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool LogAfterFailure { get; set; } = true;

    [Parameter] public string LogTitle { get; set; } = "View pull output";

    [Parameter] public string CancelTitle { get; set; } = "Cancel pull";

    [Parameter] public string DismissTitle { get; set; } = "Dismiss";

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnLog { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnCancel { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The cross of a row that ended, well or badly: forget it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnDismiss { get; set; }

    private bool Running => !Failed && !Done;
}
